WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:06.430
In this lesson, we draw a lash map, and then follow it, step by step.

00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:11.230
The example today is a soft cat eye, for a client with almond eyes.

00:00:11.749 --> 00:00:14.190
The lengths in this lesson are only an example:

00:00:14.454 --> 00:00:18.990
a real map always depends on the eyes and the natural lashes of each client.

00:00:19.578 --> 00:00:22.510
You learned how to attach each lash in the classic lesson.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.110
Today, we focus on the thinking before you attach.

00:00:26.796 --> 00:00:27.491
Step one:

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.771
consultation.

00:00:29.442 --> 00:00:32.771
The client sits up, eyes open, looking straight ahead.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.491
Look at her eye shape, look at her natural lashes, and ask what she wants.

00:00:37.751 --> 00:00:42.611
Show her example photos of a few styles, and explain which one suits her, and why.

00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:47.251
While the client is still sitting up with her eyes open, remember two landmarks:

00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:50.691
the position of the pupil, and the highest point of the eyebrow.

00:00:50.948 --> 00:00:53.736
Later, when she is lying down with her eyes closed,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:57.011
you will need these two landmarks to place the longest point.

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.971
Agree together on one style before you go on.

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.851
Never start while the client is still undecided.

00:01:03.443 --> 00:01:04.306
Step two:

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.106
preparation, as in the classic practice lesson:

00:01:07.455 --> 00:01:12.146
a comfortable position, cleansing, under eye pads, then brushing.

00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:15.746
Today, the pad must be really flat and neat.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.986
Because it will be the paper you draw the map on.

00:01:18.639 --> 00:01:19.515
Step three:

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.435
measure the natural lashes.

00:01:21.941 --> 00:01:24.764
Look at the eye straight from above, not from the side,

00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:27.435
because looking from the side gives the wrong result.

00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:31.864
In each zone, the inner corner, the middle and the outer corner,

00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:35.675
hold an extension of known length parallel to the natural lash,

00:01:35.863 --> 00:01:36.475
to compare.

00:01:36.979 --> 00:01:39.355
Some technicians use a small lash ruler.

00:01:39.551 --> 00:01:40.395
Remember well:

00:01:40.562 --> 00:01:45.355
how long the natural lashes are in each zone, and whether they are strong or weak.

00:01:45.775 --> 00:01:47.355
That is the limit of your map.

00:01:48.019 --> 00:01:48.883
Step four:

00:01:49.058 --> 00:01:50.163
mark the zones.

00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:55.892
With a fine, non toxic pen that is safe for skin, draw a few short lines on the pad,

00:01:55.842 --> 00:02:00.883
dividing the lash line from the inner corner to the outer corner into five zones.

00:02:01.238 --> 00:02:03.923
Or use printed mapping stickers, that works too.

00:02:04.352 --> 00:02:08.163
The pen touches only the pad, never the lashes, never the eye.

00:02:08.748 --> 00:02:10.450
Also mark the position of the pupil,

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.883
which you remembered while the client was sitting up.

00:02:13.198 --> 00:02:16.403
For a doll style, the longest point goes right there.

00:02:16.664 --> 00:02:20.163
For the cat eye today, the longest point is in the outer zone.

00:02:20.824 --> 00:02:21.699
Step five:

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:25.139
write the length and the curl for each zone, just under the line.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:28.019
For example, with this soft cat eye:

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:35.459
the inner corner zone 8 mm, then 9, 10, 11, and the outer zone 12 mm,

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:36.659
all with a C curl.

00:02:37.086 --> 00:02:38.899
Again, this is only an example.

00:02:39.168 --> 00:02:44.019
The length in each zone must never exceed what the natural lashes you just measured can carry.

00:02:44.228 --> 00:02:47.864
Wherever the lashes are weak, that zone gets shorter and lighter,

00:02:47.814 --> 00:02:49.299
however beautiful the map.

00:02:49.806 --> 00:02:53.931
For a fox eye, you can also write a stronger curl for the outer zone,

00:02:53.881 --> 00:02:55.939
for example switching from C to D,

00:02:56.049 --> 00:02:57.539
so the outer corner is lifted.

00:02:58.161 --> 00:02:59.060
Step six:

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.180
make the map for the other eye, as a mirror image:

00:03:02.376 --> 00:03:06.660
the inner corner is still zone one, and the outer corner still zone five.

00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:09.644
Measure the natural lashes on that side again,

00:03:09.594 --> 00:03:13.620
because two eyes are rarely identical, then adjust the lengths if needed,

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.060
so the result looks balanced.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:16.514
Step seven:

00:03:16.851 --> 00:03:19.413
arrange the lash trays in the order of the map,

00:03:19.363 --> 00:03:22.674
the shortest strip for the inner corner, then getting longer.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:27.074
Keep an extra, shorter strip ready for the baby lashes in the inner corner.

00:03:27.503 --> 00:03:29.795
That way, your hands do not have to search,

00:03:29.745 --> 00:03:32.194
and you are less likely to mix up the lengths.

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:33.471
Step eight:

00:03:33.658 --> 00:03:34.591
anchor lashes.

00:03:35.094 --> 00:03:39.551
In each zone, attach a few lashes first, at exactly the length on the map.

00:03:39.978 --> 00:03:41.551
This is the frame of the whole set.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:45.871
Looking at the anchor lashes, you can immediately see the curve of the style:

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.631
does it rise gradually toward the outer corner, is there any break in it?

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.671
Anchor lashes still follow the classic technique:

00:03:52.856 --> 00:03:56.575
isolate a single lash, the base of the extension off the eyelid,

00:03:56.525 --> 00:03:57.951
never touching the skin.

00:03:58.584 --> 00:03:59.472
Step nine:

00:03:59.679 --> 00:04:00.512
check the shape.

00:04:00.986 --> 00:04:05.685
Some salons let the client sit up for a quick look in the mirror after the anchor lashes,

00:04:05.635 --> 00:04:08.192
once the glue has set and her eyes do not sting.

00:04:08.683 --> 00:04:12.355
If your salon does this, this is the easiest moment to make changes,

00:04:12.305 --> 00:04:14.272
because there are only a few lashes.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:18.912
If not, stand at the head of the bed, look down, and compare both eyes.

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:20.348
Step ten:

00:04:20.604 --> 00:04:21.308
fill in.

00:04:21.698 --> 00:04:24.588
Attach the remaining lashes, zone by zone.

00:04:25.024 --> 00:04:30.108
Let the lengths change gradually between zones, so it stays soft, with no steps.

00:04:30.614 --> 00:04:35.114
Alternate between the zones as in the classic lesson, so the glue has time to cure,

00:04:35.064 --> 00:04:36.508
and there are no stickies.

00:04:37.165 --> 00:04:38.041
Step eleven:

00:04:38.224 --> 00:04:39.241
check the balance.

00:04:39.544 --> 00:04:43.081
Stand at the head of the bed, and look down at both eyes at once.

00:04:43.493 --> 00:04:47.081
The length at the outer corner, the longest point, the curl:

00:04:47.432 --> 00:04:49.001
are they the same on both sides?

00:04:49.575 --> 00:04:52.281
Wherever something is missing, add a few lashes.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:54.521
Then brush the lashes through once more.

00:04:55.162 --> 00:04:59.245
Before we finish, three very common mistakes when working from a map.

00:04:59.594 --> 00:05:02.780
First, measuring and drawing while looking from the side,

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.925
so the map is off right from the start.

00:05:05.476 --> 00:05:08.404
Second, copying the map exactly to the other eye,

00:05:08.354 --> 00:05:12.045
forgetting that the natural lashes on each side are different.

00:05:12.394 --> 00:05:17.485
Third, jumping too far in length between zones, so the lash line looks stepped.

00:05:17.806 --> 00:05:22.285
All three can be avoided, if you work slowly and look carefully at every step.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:26.685
Finally, remove the pads while the client's eyes are still closed,

00:05:26.635 --> 00:05:29.579
and give aftercare advice as in the classic lesson.

00:05:29.905 --> 00:05:33.019
Before the client leaves, record the map in her profile:

00:05:33.218 --> 00:05:36.059
the style, and the length and curl for each zone.

00:05:36.403 --> 00:05:39.552
At the next refill, you can do it exactly the same again,

00:05:39.502 --> 00:05:41.019
or adjust it to her wishes.

00:05:41.276 --> 00:05:43.979
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
